The Pyramid of Numbers! The number in any brick is always equal to the two bricks directly underneath it added together. What number belongs in the empty cell?
$$
\begin{array}{ccccc}
 & & \boxed{25} & & \\
 & \boxed{11} & & \boxed{14} & \\
\boxed{4} & & \boxed{?} & & \boxed{7}
\end{array}
$$

You are trapped in a dungeon! To open the exit door, you must step on the correct sequence of stones. Follow the arrows and calculate the final value at the **EXIT**:
$$
\begin{array}{ccccc}
\boxed{\text{START: } 15} & \rightarrow & \boxed{\text{Add } 7} & \rightarrow & \boxed{\text{Minus } 4} \\
& & & & \downarrow \\
\boxed{\text{EXIT: } ?} & \leftarrow & \boxed{\text{Divide by } 2} & \leftarrow & \boxed{\text{Multiply by } 3}
\end{array}
$$

An alchemist is brewing a speed potion. The recipe book shows two combinations of magical ingredients. If 1 Fire Flower ($\color{red}{\curlywedge}$) is worth 4 points, how many points is 1 Moon Grass ($\color{cyan}{\between}$) worth?
$$
\begin{array}{lcl}
\color{red}{\curlywedge} + \color{red}{\curlywedge} & = & 8 \text{ points} \\
\color{red}{\curlywedge} + \color{cyan}{\between} + \color{cyan}{\between} & = & 14 \text{ points}
\end{array}
$$

In the Smith family, every boy has exactly 2 brothers, and every girl has exactly 1 brother. If we look at just the brothers ($\color{blue}{\triangle}$) and sisters ($\color{pink}{\bigcirc}$), how many total children are in the family?
$$
\begin{array}{ccccc}
\color{blue}{\triangle} & \color{blue}{\triangle} & \color{blue}{\triangle} & \color{pink}{\bigcirc} & \dots?
\end{array}
$$

Look at this family age chart! A mother's age is equal to her two children's ages added together. A grandfather's age is equal to the mother's age multiplied by 2. How old is the Grandfather?
$$
\begin{array}{ccccc}
 & & \boxed{\text{Grandfather: ?}} & & \\
 & & \downarrow \times 2 & & \\
 & & \boxed{\text{Mother}} & & \\
 & \nearrow & & \nwarrow & \\
\boxed{\text{Brother: 12}} & & & & \boxed{\text{Sister: 18}}
\end{array}
$$
